course: dictionary
lesson: 14737
title: Long-lasting words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Prolonged means lasting a long time, or longer than usual. Look inside the word: prolong means to make something last longer, and long is right there in it. «After a prolonged silence, the teacher finally spoke.» The silence went on for longer than normal, so the word tells you how long it was.
explain: Prolonged is often used with a warning. «Prolonged exposure to the sun can burn your skin.» Exposure means being in something, and prolonged tells you it lasts a long time. A short time in the sun is usually fine, but staying out for hours is the danger.
explain: The word can also be a verb in the past tense. «The coach prolonged the practice so the team could finish the drill.» Here the coach made the practice last longer. To check, swap in a phrase such as made it last longer, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Prolonged means lasting a long time, or longer than usual.
fact: Prolong is a verb meaning to make something last longer, so prolonged is its past tense.
fact: «Prolonged silence» means a quiet that goes on and on.
fact: «Prolonged exposure» means being in something, such as sun or cold, for a long time.
fact: A good clue is the word long hidden inside prolonged.
exercise: «The hall was filled with prolonged applause.» What does prolonged applause mean? | Clapping in the rain | *Clapping that lasts a long time | Loud singing | Short and quick clapping
exercise: «Prolonged exposure to the sun can burn your skin.» What does prolonged exposure mean? | Going swimming | *Being in the sun for a long time | Looking at the sun through glasses | Sleeping under a tree
exercise: «The coach prolonged the practice so the team could finish the drill.» Find and copy the word that means made something last longer. | *prolonged | coach | team | practice
test: «A prolonged drought dried up the river.» What does prolonged drought mean? | A flood that lasts one day | A short rain shower | *A dry spell that lasts a long time | A cold, windy day
test: Mia says, «The noise was prolonged.» What does she mean? | The noise was very quiet | The noise stopped suddenly | *The noise lasted a long time | The noise came from far away
exam: «The prolonged cold made the pond freeze solid.» What does prolonged cold mean? | A cold drink on a hot day | A cold day that passes quickly | *Cold weather that lasts a long time | Cold food in the fridge
